    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "The panel collectively selects Candidate 2 (BALANCED) as the most likely to succeed. All candidates correctly ignore the outdated ATS 'Path B' directive to apply credits to unpaid base fees, recognizing that the docket XML and recent accounting records confirm all base and extension fees were already fully satisfied via a $2,388.00 remittance on October 10/13. Furthermore, the candidates brilliantly calculate the true unapplied overpayment balance to be $862.00 (adding the redundant $68.00 late surcharge paid on October 13 to the previously confirmed $794.00 in stranded credits), demonstrating exceptional statutory and accounting rigor. Candidate 2 is chosen as the winner because its closing request to 'Advance the application to the examining corps for substantive review' is the most elegant, professional, and procedurally accurate phrasing for transitioning out of pre-examination processing.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "The candidates intentionally and correctly deviate from the ATS 'Waterfall Strategy Directive: Path B' because that directive is based on an outdated assumption of unpaid base fees. The primary docket XML and the ATS summary itself confirm that the $2,388.00 payment fully satisfied all outstanding fees, rendering the Path B credit-application strategy legally moot and factually impossible. The candidates successfully execute the mandatory preemptive formalities curing (Substitute Specification excising embedded elements) and correctly demand a refund/deposit allocation of the mathematically accurate $862.00 overpayment.",
